 \label{def:multi own2 auuc} For \( k \in [K] \), define \( h_k(S_k^T, \frac{p}{100}m_k^T) \) and \( h_k(S_k^C, \frac{p}{100}m_k^C) \) as the first \( p \) percentiles of \( S_k^T \) and \( S_k^C \), respectively, when arranged according to the predictions of each \( h_k \). Furthermore, for \( S^T \) and \( S^C \), we have \( h(S^g, \frac{p}{100} n^g) = \sum_{k \in K} h_k(S_k^g, \frac{p}{100} m_k^g) \). 

